+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys live in the data
+as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`; `data/seed.json` has one per role
+(replace them before real use). No key or an unknown key is `unauthorized`
+(401); a known key without permission is `forbidden` (403).
+
+- `viewer`: GET requests only.
+- `cook`: also cook recipes, record waste, log temperatures and enter
+  stock-take counts.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+Every authenticated request that is not a GET is appended to `audit`
+(`at`, `key` name, `method`, `path`, `status`), whatever its outcome.
+`GET /audit` lists the entries newest first.
